About
This document describes the process to follow for the API server SSL Certificate renewal.

As of November 2024, all the mobile apps have certificate pinning, and any changes on the server side requires to add the new certificates in all our mobile and kiosk applications using Launch Darkly flags.

⚠️ **Next certificate expiration date: **

Middleware: September 4 2026
SPM: November 5 2026
Involved Parties
Technology Infra Ops & Support team
Channels Dev Leads for Android, iOS, and Kiosk
Process Steps
Two months before the certificates expire, the Technology Infra Ops & Support team and the Channels team should discuss the timeline for the update.
About a month prior to the expiration date of the current SSL certificates, the Technology Infra Ops & Support team will request new certificates to Akamai and SPM.
The Technology Infra Ops & Support team will send the public certificates to the Dev leads.
Dev leads will have developers add the updated certificates in Launch Darkly by following the process outlined in the wiki , validate & test.
At a minimum a week before the server update, all the mobile application will deploy the new Launch Darkly flag in the production.
Validation & Testing
Check the certificates
A quick way to verify the certificate is to run an openssl command:


$ openssl x509 -text -noout -in <certificatefile>

    
Certificate:
    Data:
        Version: 3 (0x2)
        Serial Number:
            0e:9b:f7:b9:21:fb:eb:76:2c:a9:6a:31:b3:30:84:0f
        Signature Algorithm: sha256WithRSAEncryption
        Issuer: C=US, O=DigiCert Inc, OU=www.digicert.com, CN=GeoTrust TLS RSA CA G1
        Validity
            Not Before: Oct  9 00:00:00 2024 GMT
            Not After : Oct  8 23:59:59 2025 GMT
        Subject: CN=*.test.subway.com, C=US, ST=Connecticut, L=Milford, O=Franchise World Headquarters, LLC
...
Check the Validity (here certificate expires October 8 2025 at midnight)
Check the Subject CN (here set to *.test.subway.com, our lowers API servers)
note: another tool called certtool can also be used. Check this page for more info
